{
  "id": "COMPOUND:30099 - PROTEIN:5780",
  "verbalization": "Polygonatoside A is implicated in the regulation of a sialyltransferase enzyme, CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, which is a key enzyme in the synthesis of sialic acid. This enzyme is targeted by multiple compounds, including (3aR,6S,6aR)-3,6-bis(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)-1,3,3a,4,6,6a-hexahydrofuro[3,4-c]furan and 2-Methylheptyl propanoate, both of which are linked to the activation of SQ20B. The shared target of these compounds suggests a potential mechanism of action involving the modulation of sialyltransferase activity, which could influence cellular processes related to sialylation. The evidence from the three paths indicates a consistent pathway where Polygonatoside A acts as a modulator of the sialyltransferase, which in turn affects SQ20B. The integration of these pathways supports the hypothesis that Polygonatoside A may exert its effects through a mechanism involving the regulation of sialyltransferase activity, which is a critical step in the biosynthesis of sialic acid and may have implications in cellular signaling and function.",
